  "notes": "Riff is a Spotify-desktop clone: three rounded near-black panels floating on a mid-grey (#3a3a3a) window chrome with 8px gutters, plus a full-width player bar. Album art is generative: concentric rings, diagonal stripes, blurred blobs, and sunset-horizon motifs with grain, giving a cohesive synthetic look. The right now-playing panel uses a green gradient tinted from the current artwork. Shelves overflow horizontally with the last card clipped; chevron at right of each heading is 'Show all'. Sidebar segmented control switches Playlists/Albums/Queue; sort dropdown offers Recents/Recently Added/Alphabetical/Custom. Window-control buttons (mini player, minimize, maximize, close) indicate an Electron-style desktop app. Source badges (YouTube Music red dot) mark audio provenance."
